2026-11-10T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2489) 'What numbers should the base model's body carry so clothing fits and the net can be checked?
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2489  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-10T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2489) 'The base model is the body base (the reference rig everything else hangs from). GarmentCodeData v2 (the CC BY 4.0 garment dataset) stores body measurements beside the waist and collar vertex labels. Those labels plus the mesh are all a garment needs to sit on the body. So the measurements must be re-readable from the base model alone.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2489  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-10T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2489) 'Read DETAILS for the loop definitions and the first gate.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2489  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-10T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2489) 'Extracting body measurements from the base model
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2489  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-10T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2489) 'The base model's body measurements come from the mesh itself. Circumference is the perimeter of a labeled cross-section loop. Length is a geodesic distance between two landmarks. GarmentCodeData v2 supplies the waist and collar vertex labels that anchor them. RFD66606-2488 (cage-wrapped surface net) reproduces those same labels. So measuring the base model is also a check that the net read the parts correctly.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2489  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-10T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2489) '- RFD66606-2488, the cage-wrapped surface net whose part labels this RFD reads.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2489  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-10T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2489) '- RFD66606-2424, the anthropometric keypoint fit whose landmark vocabulary this inherits.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2489  1 LINE
 Text:Written

